<title>USA: Entergy says 936 MW River Bend back on line Thursday.</title>
<headline>Entergy says 936 MW River Bend back on line Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entergy Corp plans to have its 936 megawatt (MW) River Bend nuclear power plant reconnected to the power grid Thursday, the company said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The unit was shut May 6 to repair a flow control valve.  </p>
<p>&quot;The necessary maintenance has been completed, and the plant should be synchronizing to the grid sometime tomorrow,&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Following last week's shutdown, the company had reported that the unit would likely be down for one to two weeks.</p>
<p>The River Bend plant is located in St Francisville, La.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
